 + (\ell_1{-}\ell_2)\,p(1{-}p)\left(\frac{\partial\ell_1}{\partial\mathbf{h}}\right)^{\!\top}\mathbf{w}\Bigg]
\end{multline*}
The first term (self-gradient) always decreases $\ell_1$. The second (cross-gradient) is negligible when expert gradients are approximately orthogonal, a condition that holds empirically once experts specialize to distinct input clusters. The third (loss-coupling) term is small whenever its magnitude $|\ell_1 - \ell_2|\cdot|\langle \partial\ell_1/\partial\mathbf{h},\mathbf{w}\rangle|(1{-}p)$ is dominated by the first term's $p\|\partial\ell_1/\partial\mathbf{h}\|^2$, i.e., when the dimensionless ratio
